## 🚫 CRITICAL RESTRICTIONS

### NEVER DO:
1. **NO realistic human faces/eyes in avatar** (Islamic guideline violation)
2. **NO unlimited free access** (business suicide)
3. **NO storing API keys in frontend** (security breach)
4. **NO generic fonts** (Inter, Roboto, Arial = lazy design)
5. **NO purple gradients on white** (AI slop aesthetic)
6. **NO skipping email verification** (spam/abuse magnet)
7. **NO complex onboarding** (< 2 minutes to first conversation)
8. **NO unvalidated Arabic text** (encoding issues, mojibake)

### ALWAYS DO:
1. **RTL support** for Arabic text (dir="rtl")
2. **Validate Stripe webhooks** (payment security)
3. **Rate limit ALL API routes** (prevent abuse)
4. **Log corrections** in database (analytics gold)
5. **Cache common responses** (save API costs)
6. **Error boundaries** around AI calls (graceful failures)
7. **Accessibility** (ARIA labels, keyboard navigation)
8. **Mobile-first design** (primary usage device)

---

## 📝 CODING STANDARDS

### TypeScript
```typescript
// Strict mode enabled
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "strict": true,
    "noImplicitAny": true,
    "strictNullChecks": true
  }
}

// All functions typed
function sendMessage(
  content: string, 
  userId: string, 
  scenarioId: string
): Promise<ConversationResponse> {
  // ...
}

// No 'any' types allowed (use 'unknown' if truly dynamic)
```

### Component Structure
```tsx
// Functional components with TypeScript
interface ChatInterfaceProps {
  scenarioId: string;
  userLevel: Level;
  language: Language;
}

export function ChatInterface({ 
  scenarioId, 
  userLevel, 
  language 
}: ChatInterfaceProps) {
  // Hooks at top
  const [messages, setMessages] = useState<Message[]>([]);
  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(false);
  
  // Event handlers
  const handleSendMessage = async (content: string) => {
    // ...
  };
  
  // Render
  return (
    <div className="chat-container">
      {/* ... */}
    </div>
  );
}
```

### API Routes
```typescript
// app/api/chat/route.ts
import { NextRequest, NextResponse } from 'next/server';

export async function POST(req: NextRequest) {
  try {
    // 1. Authenticate user
    const user = await authenticate(req);
    
    // 2. Validate request body
    const { message, scenarioId, language } = await req.json();
    
    // 3. Check rate limits
    await checkRateLimits(user.id, user.plan);
    
    // 4. Call Claude API
    const response = await generateResponse(message, scenarioId, language, user.level);
    
    // 5. Save to database
    await saveConversation(user.id, message, response);
    
    // 6. Return response
    return NextResponse.json({ success: true, response });
    
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Chat API error:', error);
    return NextResponse.json(
      { error: error.message }, 
      { status: error.status || 500 }
    );
  }
}
```

### CSS/Tailwind
```tsx
// Use Tailwind utilities, custom CSS only for complex animations
<div className="
  flex flex-col h-screen
  bg-gradient-to-br from-primary-night to-neutral-warm-gray
  text-neutral-sand
  rtl:text-right ltr:text-left
">
  {/* Arabic text auto-RTL */}
  <p className="font-arabic-body text-lg" dir="rtl">
    مرحبا بك في التطبيق
  </p>
</div>

// Custom CSS only for what Tailwind can't do
@keyframes avatar-pulse {
  0%, 100% { opacity: 1; transform: scale(1); }
  50% { opacity: 0.8; transform: scale(1.05); }
}

.avatar-speaking {
  animation: avatar-pulse 2s ease-in-out infinite;
}
```

